<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Biryawaza</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">14th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century-bce">14th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Biryawaza was a ruler in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> in the 14th century BCE, known from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amarna-letters">Amarna letters</a>, the diplomatic correspondence of the Egyptian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">pharaohs</a>. Based in the land of Upi around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a>, he served as an Egyptian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> and agent, opposing the expansion of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hittite-empire">Hittites</a> and their allies, such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aitakkama">Aitakkama</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kadesh">Kadesh</a>, and became involved in the quarrels of other Canaanite rulers.</p></div>
